From 6b7fa60eeeea19bc2c13172971c34fa9d301ac18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:08:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Offer a one-time restart for anti-cheat games in Plasma Leave

Add "Restart for anti-cheat games" as the second entry of Restart Options, in Kickoff and in KRunner. It is offered on a UEFI start when sparky-stereo-boot has written its anti-cheat GRUB entry and GRUB can be told to start it once (the boot package keeps /var/lib/sparky-stereo-boot/anticheat.entry only then). Every path opens a confirmation that says what the start does and lists what Easy Anti-Cheat would not accept on this computer, from sparky-stereo-boot's checker in the session's language. Confirming asks the boot package's polkit-guarded helper, through pkexec, to start that entry once before the session closes; a refusal is said in the greeter, and a cancelled logout takes the one-time start back. Rows the anti-cheat start settles by its own kernel line (lockdown, kexec; sparky-stereo-boot marks them settledByAntiCheatStart) are left out, and when the rows would push the buttons past the screen the confirmation moves up and the avatar steps aside.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)
